    - llvm_ir  # 8389
    isbefore: []  # 8389
    duplicate_of: []  # 8389
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8389
    pr_ref:  # 8389
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-20 docstring-staleness audit (verifier reproduced in four scratch dirs). `_resolve_calls` short-circuits only on a local symbol of kind function; a local `declare` (kind declaration) falls through to the repo-wide registry, which is last-wins by bare name (analyze/base.py ~L4069). So when a.ll declares @puts and def.ll defines it, main -> puts resolves to def.ll's define if a.ll registers first, and to a.ll's own declaration otherwise: output differs across checkouts. Fix: LlvmIrAnalyzer.register_symbol must not let a declaration overwrite a function of the same name."  # 8389
    fields: {}  # 8389
